            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The candidate adds checkReviewStopHook to engine/status/status.go. It reuses the beforeEntries guard, so unreadable settings fail and absent settings warn, the same as the neighbouring family checks. Missing or drifted entries warn and name the fix.",
              "Status behavior is covered at several levels. The status unit tests cover missing, edited, and foreign-program Stop entries, and a different binary path. The goldens cover the empty-home, no-home, invalid-JSON, directory, and drifted-settings cases.",
              "Runtime adapter tests cover install, partial status on a pre-existing install, drift repair via Update, and uninstall that keeps foreign Stop entries. A golden covers the runtime status and update flow for a removed Stop entry.",
              "The declarations test pins the capability claim wording and its referenced test names.",
              "The patch contains only the status check and test changes. It has no settings.MissingReviewStopHookParts implementation or install and uninstall code, so I could not verify the underlying behavior. This is outside the visible candidate and is not a reliability finding.",
              "I found no regressions on valid baseline input. The only changes to existing output are the added Stop check line and the updated check count."
